1
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for that day
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:34,000
I kicked a pebble and my shoes flew off too,

3
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:42,300
right onto the head of the
carpenter I'd been saving money with.

4
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:55,280
Even if I somehow rouse my spirit,
it's Katsushika, always.

6
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,560
Even the yawn-inducing,
unchanged streetscape feels oddly kind.

7
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:14,640
From the pointed hat's water
jug up to the vast heavens,

8
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls.

9
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow, too,
somehow it will end, won't it?

10
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,040
Only winning... Shibamata...
happiness again, they say.

11
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,740
I only realized it after I lost it.

12
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:33,840
Because I'm such a fool.

13
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:40,700
Don't call me Papa.

14
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:01,980
It's a baby.

15
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,380
What? Where did you come from?

16
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,020
Someone?

17
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:14,640
What on earth are parents
thinking these days?

18
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,060
Leaving a source of noise like
this in front of the police box!

19
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:20,280
I can't even take a proper nap!

20
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,500
He's laughing.

21
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:34,740
Is there something on my face?

22
00:02:34,740 --> 00:02:35,200
Good morning.

23
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,220
Reiko.

24
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:39,300
What a cute baby!

25
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,680
Whose baby?

26
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:42,800
That's the lost property.

27
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,540
It seems no missing person
report has been filed.

28
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:49,600
Could it be an abandoned child after all?

29
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:52,080
Abandoning such an adorable baby...

30
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,200
I can't believe it.

31
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,680
You don't know who left it here?

32
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:57,820
They were probably dozing off, I bet.

33
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:58,540
*Gulp*

34
00:02:58,540 --> 00:03:03,160
Right when emergency calls and
lost-item reports were pouring in...

35
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:04,700
Don't lie.

36
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:07,340
You can't even manage to
mind the place properly.

37
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:08,920
You're useless.

38
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:10,600
Shh... shh...

39
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:12,280
What?

40
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,320
Shh... shh...

41
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:16,200
It sounds like it's saying "shee shee."

42
00:03:16,620 --> 00:03:18,460
Isn't its diaper wet?

43
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:22,100
I think there were disposable diapers in the cart,
if I recall.

44
00:03:22,820 --> 00:03:24,500
These? Let's see, let's see.

45
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:26,600
Yes.

46
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,360
Oh my

47
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:33,660
There, there,
that was uncomfortable, wasn't it?

48
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,160
You're really quick with that, Chief.

49
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:40,980
Whenever my grandson Daisuke comes over,
I'm always the one changing his diapers.

50
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:42,380
What is it?

51
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,700
It's like a letter.
It came out from under the diaper.

52
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:47,480
I'm going to read it.

53
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:49,660
This child is your son.

54
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:51,880
Please take care of Taro
until I come to pick him up.

55
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,800
So this baby's name is Taro

56
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:58,060
Didn't you say he was your son?

57
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,260
Now that you mention it...

58
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:00,700
Kazue

59
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:07,300
So that means one of us
here is Taro's father?

60
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,440
Who is it? Come clean and tell the truth.

61
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,380
Going by likelihood,

62
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:17,160
You suspect me?

63
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,640
After all, Nakagawa,
even if he just keeps quiet,

64
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:23,620
women come chasing after him.
He's a total ladies' man.

65
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:26,320
It wouldn't be strange if
he had ten or twenty kids.

66
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:29,140
Please don't call me a gigolo, Senpai.

67
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:31,260
Nakagawa, look me in the eye.

68
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:33,500
Do you really have no
recollection of it at all?

69
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:36,020
No, I don't.

70
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,340
Alright, Nakagawa's innocent.

71
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:47,020
Hey, you're really going
to believe that, Chief?

72
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:50,080
My instincts as a police officer never fail.

73
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:52,160
When I say he's innocent, he's innocent.

74
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,420
Kei-chan isn't the kind of person
who'd do something so sneaky.

75
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:56,980
That's right, Ryo-san.

76
00:04:58,820 --> 00:04:59,860
What?

77
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,280
Rather than someone who's used
to playing around like Nakagawa,

78
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:06,020
it's often the dead-serious type like
Terai who turns out to be the real culprit.

79
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:07,360
See?

80
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:10,540
Doesn't his nose look a bit like yours?

81
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:11,840
Ryo-san.

82
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,800
Confess quickly and make it
easier on yourself, Terai.

83
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:18,680
I-I-I would never cheat on anyone, you know?

84
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:21,360
Come on, look me in the eye.

85
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:22,300
Chief.

86
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:33,020
Shiro, these eyes belong to an
honest man who can't tell a lie.

87
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,180
Thank you, Chief.

88
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:40,340
No, it may be the one and only mistake
an honest man who can't lie has made.

89
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:43,080
Ryo-san, if you keep this up,
I'll get angry too.

90
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:46,340
In that case, that leaves the Chief.

91
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:47,460
Yes.

92
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:48,040
What?

93
00:05:48,980 --> 00:05:51,200
Suspecting Chief Ohara like that!

94
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,400
Yeah, Ryo-chan,
that's a bit much, don't you think?

95
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,980
I have grandchildren, you know!

96
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:02,400
In cases like this, the person everyone thinks couldn't
possibly be the culprit is very likely the real culprit.

97
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:04,400
When you put it that way,

98
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,140
no way...

99
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:07,400
not the Chief, surely.

100
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:12,200
What's with that suspicious
look on your face?

101
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:14,940
Nowadays there are all sorts of drugs,
you know.

102
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:17,360
Just because he's an old man doesn't
mean you can underestimate him.

103
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,480
Don't talk such nonsense.

104
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,680
Did I startle you? Sorry about that.

105
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,460
Chief, look me in the eye.

106
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:27,980
What?

107
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:31,400
If you have nothing to hide,
you shouldn't have anything to fear.

108
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,440
Of course. Bring it on.

109
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,480
His eyes are moving suspiciously.

110
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:42,520
It's because you're all in this together.

111
00:06:43,260 --> 00:06:44,940
I don't think it's the Chief.

112
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:46,540
I think so too.

113
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,180
Yeah.

114
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:49,160
Thank you, thank you.

115
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,980
It was just getting interesting.

116
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:58,380
So what about you? Well, the Chief is still a suspect,
isn't he? Yeah, that's right.

117
00:06:58,380 --> 00:07:06,640
You're a suspect too, senpai! Can you prove I had nothing to do with it?
Look into these innocent eyes that can't lie.

118
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:18,020
There's not a trace of truth in those eyes. They're a big liar's eyes.
Yeah, those are the eyes of someone dodging responsibility. Those eyes are beneath contempt for a man.

119
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:21,420
You're all ganging up together.
That's cowardly!

120
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:26,080
Ryo-chan, you always shout when
things go badly for you, don't you?

121
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:26,580
Yeah.

122
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:29,340
Papa!

123
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,320
He just said "Papa"!

124
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,760
He looked at Ryo-san's face and said "Papa"!

125
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:37,580
I heard it too! Me too!

126
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,120
Here you go, Ryo-chan.

127
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,000
That's ridiculous!

128
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:43,220
Papa!

129
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:45,880
Hey! Don't say such slanderous things!

130
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:46,620
Papa!

131
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:52,202
At this age, babies can only say
"Mama" and "Papa,"

132
00:07:52,252 --> 00:07:54,180
so of course it's
"Papa, Papa" no matter who they look at.

133
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:58,040
Sunamatsu!

134
00:07:58,080 --> 00:07:58,920
What?

135
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,280
That's ridiculous!

136
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,840
Ryotsu! What a cowardly man you are!

137
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:09,180
No, it's not like that!

138
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:13,592
Those joined eyebrows are proof enough!
Stop being so stubborn!

139
00:08:13,642 --> 00:08:14,460
Ryotsu!

140
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:17,520
It's the truth,
I have no memory of it at all!

141
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:19,160
I don't know anything, Chief.

142
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:25,960
Until the mother comes back, you'll take responsibility
as a man and a father and look after that child!

143
00:08:26,460 --> 00:08:27,620
You can go home for today.

144
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:28,560
No way...

145
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:30,120
Papa

146
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:33,180
I'm not the father! I'm being framed!

147
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,140
Good work.

148
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:38,900
Will he be all right?

149
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:41,960
Ryo-san, isn't it too much to take
care of a baby all of a sudden?

150
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:45,200
Even if he's the father, poor Taro-kun.

151
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:47,720
Wait, Ryo-chan! I'm coming with you.

152
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:56,200
Which diapers should I get, Papa?

153
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:58,920
One you'll never have to change
for the rest of your life.

154
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:00,900
Don't be ridiculous, there's no such thing.

155
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:04,200
Why do I have to go through this?

156
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:06,620
What a cute little boy.

157
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:08,760
He looks just like his father.

158
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,500
He's not my child, is he?

159
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:12,500
Papa!

160
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:16,040
See, even the baby is calling you Papa.

161
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:19,396
You're always joking. Stop it,

162
00:09:19,446 --> 00:09:22,000
you're the father,
you have to pull yourself together.

163
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:24,300
Don't give me any of your lip, Papa.

164
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,598
Ryo-chan,

165
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:28,900
in situations like this,
you should just go along with it.

166
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:32,080
This is all your fault for calling me
"Papa" in the first place.

167
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,060
But that's what you are, isn't it?

168
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:34,960
No!

169
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,280
Papa!

170
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:37,120
No!

171
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,220
Papa!

172
00:09:38,980 --> 00:09:40,940
Heh heh, this is a nightmare.

173
00:09:48,100 --> 00:09:50,480
It was such a mess,
so I took the liberty of tidying up.

174
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:53,560
My model kits, my games...

175
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:55,640
Good evening, Auntie.

176
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:56,860
Welcome.

177
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:02,180
The Chief called me to say Ryo-san was bringing
a baby home and asked me to look after things.

178
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,560
I was flustered.

179
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:07,240
This room was an absolute disaster,
you know.

180
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,480
With you here, Auntie, we can rest easy.

181
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:12,260
Now then, Taro-kun, this is your home.

182
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:13,620
Welcome.

183
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:18,680
Oh my, what a strong baby.

184
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:23,360
Triangle Robo,
so you made it through unharmed.

185
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:24,780
There, there.

186
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:29,080
Hey, don't break it.

187
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:32,640
With this place,
at least Taro won't lack for toys.

188
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,780
It's not just any toy.

189
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:38,960
It was modeled after the Triangle Robot from
Shōnen Jet that I used to watch when I was a kid.

190
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,600
It's the robot of the late Yonezawa.

191
00:10:42,260 --> 00:10:45,160
Ryo-san, you're a father now, you know.

192
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,340
This is no time to be playing with toys.

193
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,720
I keep telling you, he's not my kid.

194
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,980
Hey, that's not food! Give it back!

195
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,540
The little guy must be hungry.

196
00:10:57,540 --> 00:10:59,600
I'll get dinner ready, so...

197
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,900
Ryo-san, you give Taro a bath.

198
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:05,940
Well, good luck, Papa.

199
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:06,840
Reiko.

200
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:11,820
Why won't you call her "Mama," you?

201
00:11:11,820 --> 00:11:12,540
Papa.

202
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:16,000
Papa

203
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,660
That doesn't make any sense.

204
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:21,040
If you're blamed for someone else's mistake,
at least try saying thanks.

205
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,920
That kid is Ryo-san's secret child.

206
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:28,120
I heard his secret wife racked up
debts and ran off with a young man.

207
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,540
The story keeps getting bigger.

208
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:34,520
Alright, I'm going in one last time.

209
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,460
Come on, scoot over.

210
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,240
So today it's with bath salts?

211
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,520
This is nice.

212
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:50,920
I like that tingly scent.

213
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,620
Ryo-san, are you getting out already?

214
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:55,460
Staying in too long is bad for your body,
you know.

215
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:57,080
Take your time.

216
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:11,080
What the hell, Auntie, you're
treating me way differently from them!

217
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:14,440
They always say children are a blessing,
don't they?

218
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:18,420
Don't joke with me! I've been run
ragged by this kid since morning!

219
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:22,820
If his real parents show up, I'm going
to charge them a fortune for babysitting!

220
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:27,860
Fine, I'll give you this one for free,
so you'd better take good care of him.

221
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,880
That's more like it.

222
00:12:31,060 --> 00:12:33,460
As expected of you, Auntie, you understand.

223
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:35,540
A drink after the bath, cheers!

224
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,240
What is this?

225
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,320
Waaah! Waaah! Waaah! Waaah!

226
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:44,980
He's got the same mischievous streak, too.

227
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:52,220
Hey, it's eleven o'clock already,
go to sleep, already!

228
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:54,700
Jeju.

229
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:57,160
Are you a magician or something?
Go to sleep!

230
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:20,400


231
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,380
Damn it, I'll get back at him.

232
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,280
What is this?

233
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,300
Taro!

234
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:50,660
Ryo-san!

235
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,600
This is going to be an all-nighter,
isn't it.

236
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,780
Where the hell did Taro go?

237
00:13:56,760 --> 00:13:57,880
Out front, Ryo-san.

238
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:02,020
Taro! Where are you, Taro!

239
00:14:03,440 --> 00:14:03,980
Papa!

240
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,780
So you're the father?
That was brand new, you know!

241
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,040
Think you'll pay for it?

242
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:12,760
W-what?!

243
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,300
Waaaaah!

244
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,500
You ungrateful brat!

245
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:24,260
Listen, we may have the same eyebrows,
but you and I are complete strangers.

246
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:26,040
Don't they say,
"a stranger who just looks alike"?

247
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:30,600
So I have no obligation or
responsibility to raise you at all.

248
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:31,660
Got it?

249
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:32,280
Hey.

250
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:37,060
After all the help you've gotten from people,
at least say thank you.

251
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:38,340
Ugh.

252
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,420
Shut up! Just get lost!

253
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:43,160
Granny.

254
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:44,920
I'm done! I don't care anymore!

255
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:48,000
I figured you were just a harmless baby,
and look how cocky you've gotten!

256
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,220
Hey! Taro!

257
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,720
Hey! Where do you think you're going?!

258
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:06,060
Somebody! Stop that carriage!

259
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:17,620
That floppy disk,

260
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,000
it's right here.

261
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,420
It's in here.

262
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,400
The people in the car
are starting to notice.

263
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:25,220
I want this to be a one-time thing.

264
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,700
Don't get cocky.

265
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:27,920
This is the deal.

266
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:29,940
The people in the car are paying you plenty,
aren't they?

267
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:35,120
What's wrong?

268
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,260
It's gone.

269
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:37,660
It's that carriage.

270
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:42,340
What are you doing? Go after it!

271
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,120
Money!

272
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,360
Taro!

273
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:46,240
Switch over!

274
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:46,720
Uh-oh!

275
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,840
Hey, Orzo, get on!

276
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:57,920
Someone, stop that carriage!

277
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:11,980
That's in the way.

278
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:16,920
Did you see a carriage?

279
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,860
Over there!

280
00:16:17,860 --> 00:16:19,380
Thanks

281
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:35,520
Hey, did you see a baby?

282
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:36,820
No way.

283
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:38,120
Bardan!

284
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:43,000
Why would it be in a place like that?

285
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,480
Is there no other way?

286
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,300
Stairs it is, there's no choice.

287
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,220
A cop's brat

288
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:51,540
We have to get it back first,
or we're in trouble.

289
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:00,440
It's heavy.

290
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:01,460
I'll help.

291
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:05,240
Watch out!

292
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,180
Are you okay?

293
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:12,540
Never mind that, the kid!

294
00:17:12,540 --> 00:17:13,440
Got it.

295
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:34,260
Taro, don't move!

296
00:17:35,280 --> 00:18:02,500
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

297
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,260
Are you all right?

298
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:05,880
Somehow.

299
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:07,840
When did it happen?

300
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:09,400
This is mine.

301
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,540
It's mine.

302
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,140
Stop that dump truck!

303
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:26,040
There it is!

304
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:27,480
Wrong one?

305
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:30,360
This isn't the robot I brought.

306
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:32,120
So the brat's still...

307
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:33,260
Let's go!

308
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:50,560
Let's just stop this.

309
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:53,000
Things like this are a real problem.

310
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:53,900
Don't mess around!

311
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,060
If you think about it,

312
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:57,080
this all started on your land, didn't it?

313
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,120
Hey, call the police!

314
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,740
Are you trying to get us killed, you idiot?

315
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:17,160
But...

316
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:20,220
Forget it! Contact the police on the radio.

317
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,160
Some weirdo hijacked the trailer on me!

318
00:19:23,540 --> 00:19:24,640
Please, somebody help!

319
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:25,220
No, that's not it!

320
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:27,180
That dump truck!

321
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:29,160
We're tracking a sedan
on some strange route!

322
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:35,500
Call for backup! Get the cop's kid out of there.
I have nothing to do with this!

323
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:41,680
It's very much your business. You're just as guilty!
If you don't get it back, you're a dead man!

324
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:44,920
What? Were you dozing off?

325
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:49,020
There's a baby in there, you know!

326
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:52,620
Aaaaaah!

327
00:19:52,620 --> 00:19:56,060
Aaaaaah!

328
00:19:58,740 --> 00:20:06,720
!

329
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:07,080
Thank goodness.

330
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:12,720
It's little Taro!

331
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:13,740
Ryo-chan.

332
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:14,380
Senpai.

333
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:15,500
Chief.

334
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:16,600
Nakagawa, Reiko.

335
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:19,260
He seems fine, he's not hurt.

336
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:21,180
Aren't you going to worry about me?

337
00:20:21,180 --> 00:20:23,960
Ryo-chan's getting a lecture from the Chief.

338
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:27,100
Senpai, as a father,
you need to reflect on yourself.

339
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:30,480
Honestly,
putting a baby through this kind of danger!

340
00:20:30,480 --> 00:20:31,340
You idiot!

341
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:34,400
We're the ones who went through hell, Chief.

342
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,420
No.

343
00:20:36,720 --> 00:20:37,340
Hey ow!

344
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,420
What happened to the robot?

345
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:42,720
This isn't my robot, is it?

346
00:20:43,140 --> 00:20:44,620
There's a gap in a place like this.

347
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,120
What's this floppy disk?

348
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,240
Robot-san, actually...

349
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:52,240
Found it, it's the floppy disk.

350
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:58,220
Those two had already been hired as industrial
spies at the Metropolitan Police Department.

351
00:20:58,760 --> 00:20:59,680
And this is also

352
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,220
It's yours, sir.

353
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:03,660
You did a great job.

354
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:07,760
Yeah, well, I just did what
any police officer should do.

355
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:10,380
I knew they were criminals
the moment I saw them.

356
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:14,100
Isn't it just that it turned
out this way by pure chance?

357
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:17,240
Yeah, well, that's part of my skill too.

358
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:17,900
Papa

359
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:21,280
Seriously?

360
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:28,740
Taro's award ceremony ended ages ago,
didn't it?

361
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:31,340
It's true.
Ryo-chan and the others are taking forever.

362
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:32,860
They're back.

363
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,500
What's that?

364
00:21:36,880 --> 00:21:41,000
We'd really love for Taro-kun to appear
in our company's diaper commercial.

365
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,060
For now, as a contract fee, 100 million.

366
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:45,100
I see, 100 million.

367
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:46,680
And what about yours?

368
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:50,500
We'd like Taro-kun to
appear in our new TV program.

369
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:52,360
Co-starring Ryoko Hirose-chan.

370
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:53,780
I see, I see.

371
00:21:54,660 --> 00:21:57,200
Ryoko-chan's totally acting
like Taro-kun's manager now.

372
00:21:57,600 --> 00:22:00,440
So in the end, senior,
you're turning love into money.

373
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:02,020
Don't look down on me.

374
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:03,080
I see, I see.

375
00:22:03,660 --> 00:22:05,240
So, who's next?

376
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:09,460
Taro-kun's parents have been found!

377
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:16,680
It-it's connected!

378
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:17,860
Whoa, whoa.

379
00:22:24,580 --> 00:22:26,060
Taro!

380
00:22:26,060 --> 00:22:29,180
Waaah, waaah, waaah!

381
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:31,020
Waaah, waaah, waaah!

382
00:22:31,020 --> 00:22:32,820
Waaah, waaah, waaah, waaah!

383
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:33,360
Waaah, waaah, waaah!

384
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:36,680
Taro!

385
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:37,540
Mama!

386
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:40,240
Thank goodness, I'm sorry, Taro.

387
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:41,060
Mama!

388
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:44,000
Look at you, you can say "Mama" after all.

389
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:48,620
Why did you abandon him?

390
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:49,680
I didn't abandon him.

391
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:53,210
We divorced shortly after Taro was born,

392
00:22:53,260 --> 00:22:55,560
and she took custody of Taro.

393
00:22:57,100 --> 00:23:00,067
But I lost the confidence
to raise him on my own,

394
00:23:00,117 --> 00:23:04,140
so I left Taro in front
of this man's apartment.

395
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:07,440
But the carriage was in
front of the police box

396
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:11,900
My apartment is three doors
down from this police box.

397
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:15,840
It may have rolled over here somehow.

398
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:19,820
I saw this morning's news,
was shocked, and contacted him.

399
00:23:19,820 --> 00:23:21,360
It's an embarrassing story.

400
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:24,040
Thank you so much.

401
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:29,920
Taro! You forgot something!

402
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:38,900
Huff, huff, huff...

403
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:40,520
Whoa, watch out!

404
00:23:42,940 --> 00:23:43,700
Taro.

405
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:45,760
Waa-waa, baa-baa.

406
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:52,320
Waa-waa!

407
00:23:52,900 --> 00:23:55,940
Taro! Come visit again!

408
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:20,140
Even at midnight, the calls come in

409
00:24:20,140 --> 00:24:27,400
If it's you, I wake up in a good mood

410
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:31,800
Even boring stories

411
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:36,600
heat up my whole body

412
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:43,180
But I want to see my friends

413
00:24:43,180 --> 00:24:47,300
I surely want to be loved

414
00:24:47,720 --> 00:24:52,680
to the point that
everyone teases me a little

415
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:58,360
with the feeling of melting together

416
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:02,200
I surely want to confess

417
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:08,040
Somehow, only in love I'm timid

418
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:15,880
Don't hide everything about the
future I bravely pretend about

419
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,900
Personal matter: Sakonji Tatsunosuke

420
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:24,940
bidding farewell to my life in Japan

421
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:28,000
I intend to start a new life in America

422
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:31,540
For that, Saori, I must forget you

423
00:25:31,940 --> 00:25:34,720
Next time: Sakonji, a new departure

424
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:36,640
Forgive me, Saori

